event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":89,"item_id":"rs_02d033b0c9f324ad016aca55548e5481938a365d5946ef820b","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering program creation**\n\nI'm thinking about how to approach avoiding a massive recall when replacing combined routes. It seems like the easiest way might be to create a program that edits JSON scripts through bash. I realize I could use an editing approach that focuses on partial edits first, starting with the top and then moving to the backend. Hm, I wonder how efficiently that will work in practice. There’s a lot to consider in streamlining this process!"}

